 =====================================================================================================
 Frozen Density Embedding to include enviroment effects using the fixed potential method described in:
 A.S.P. Gomes, C. R. Jacob and L. Visscher, Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys. 10 (2008) 5353–5362.
 =====================================================================================================

  Frozen Density Embedding Calculation set-up:
  --------------------------------------------

 * Print level               :     0
 * Kinetic energy functional : kin_tf              
   if .ALDA is set, will use : tf_kin              
 * FDE Potential read from file: EMBPOT                                                      
 * Fixed embedding potential will be used
 * Density (and gradient) from frozen subsystems read from file: FRZDNS                                                      


   Kohn-Sham calculation set-up
   ----------------------------

 * Print level:     2
 * Numerical integration grid:
   - radial quadrature according to R. Lindh, P.-Aa. Malmqvist, and L. Gagliardi
     precision of radial quadrature set to:  0.10000E-12
   - angular quadrature using the Lebedev scheme, exact up to order L = 41
   - accepted error in integrated number of electrons:  0.10000E-02
 * DFT thresholds:
   - dfthr0 =  0.10000E-08
   - dfthri =  0.20000E-11
 * Spin density contribution in response calculations:
   - use the norm of the spin magnetization vector as a definition of the spin density (noncollinear definition)


